+## Amended in session 15c
+
+**A plan left unanswered ends `set aside`**, the seventh ending, written the moment it happens:
+
+- a new ask over a plan the user asked for: the new run follows it in the same negotiation;
+- a report of the day an open adaptation adapts: the adaptation could no longer be written.
+
+Not `stopped`, which is a run halted before it offered anything. A tap on a plan set aside writes nothing and is said as superseded. An entrance turn that handed off is the subgraph's run, read on that subgraph's thread and never as a live run of its own.
+
 ## Consequences
 
 - **`record.Run` goes.** The model, provider and budget carried in the run's config were the identity of a run answered by one model; the model belongs to the node that did the work and goes in the record's node entries.
